Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 02:14:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] feat(source-folders): "Full import" button runs the
 /update-brain importer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds full parity with the /update-brain skill to the in-app Sync panel: a
"Full import (code)" button that imports ALL file types, not just markdown.

- New project_import module shells out to the skill's OWN importer
  (scripts/import_project_vault.py) for each enabled source folder, so code
  /html/binary files become .neurovault.md sidecars byte-identically to the
  skill — the in-app import and the skill never conflict on a brain. Then it
  ingests the vault (dotfolders skipped, same as /api/update) so the new
  sidecars are searchable. Preserves the brain's display name; finds python
  on PATH (python/python3/py) and locates the script via cwd/exe/env.
- POST /api/brains/:id/sources/full_import + FullImportReport.
- Panel gets a "Full import (code)" button beside "Sync now"; store gets
  fullImportSources().
- Requires Python (same dependency the /update-brain skill already needs);
  the pure-Rust markdown Sync path is unchanged.

Verified on a throwaway brain: code files wrapped as sidecars, node_modules
excluded, everything ingested, and a re-run is idempotent (no duplication).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
